--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ABSTRACT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Hodge Complex Standard Model identifies the 14 modes at the self-paired
eigenvalue lambda = 4 of the discrete Laplacian on the periodic 8x8 torus
with one Standard Model generation. This paper establishes the spectral
content of that multiplet. We prove that the self-paired eigenvalue is
lambda = 4 with multiplicity 2(L-1) = 14; that the 14 modes decompose under
the D4 point group into three orbits of sizes (2, 8, 4); that the three
orbits carry the support classes {64, 48, 32} = {N, V, N/2}; that the
inverse participation ratios are {2/128, 3/128, 4/128}; and that the Shannon
entropy classes are {6.0, 5.5, 5.0} bits with equal spacing 0.5 bits. The
affine entropy-IPR relation S = log2(N) + 1 - N * IPR is proved as a theorem
for modes whose squared amplitudes take values in {0, 1/N, 2/N}, and this
precondition is verified for the 14 modes of the multiplet. The
identification of the 14 modes with one Standard Model generation, and the
assignment of an N/4 mass label to each mode, are the framework's empirical
thesis (HCSM-23) and are stated as disclosed inputs. All numerical claims
are verified at machine precision.

