  (2) The explicit mode list.
  (3) The D4 orbit decomposition.
  (4) The orbit stabilizer orders.
  (5) The support classes {64, 48, 32}.
  (6) The IPRs {2/128, 3/128, 4/128}.
  (7) The amplitude-value precondition |phi|^2 in {0, 1/N, 2/N}.
  (8) The affine entropy-IPR relation.
  (9) The entropy classes {6.0, 5.5, 5.0} bits.
  (10) The equal spacing 0.5 bits.
  (11) The Hodge lift 14 + 28 + 14 = 56.

Running 12-VERIFICATION/run_all.py reproduces every numerical claim in the
HCSM paper stack.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
12. CONCLUSION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This paper has established the 14-mode multiplet at the self-paired
eigenvalue lambda = 4 of the discrete Laplacian on the periodic 8x8 torus.
The self-paired eigenvalue has multiplicity 2(L-1) = 14. The 14 modes
decompose under D4 into three orbits of sizes (2, 8, 4) with stabilizer
orders 4, 1, 2.

The three orbits carry the support classes {64, 48, 32} = {N, V, N/2}, the
inverse participation ratios {2/128, 3/128, 4/128}, and the Shannon entropy
classes {6.0, 5.5, 5.0} bits with equal spacing 0.5 bits. The affine
entropy-IPR relation S = log2(N) + 1 - N * IPR is proved as a theorem for
modes whose squared amplitudes lie in {0, 1/N, 2/N}, and this precondition
is verified for every mode in the multiplet.

The identification of the 14 modes with one Standard Model generation, and
the assignment of an N/4 mass label to each mode, are the framework's
empirical thesis (HCSM-23).

