                  self-paired eigenvalue lambda = 4 of the discrete
                  Laplacian on the periodic 8x8 torus. The self-paired
                  eigenvalue has multiplicity 2(L-1) = 14 at L = 8. The
                  14 modes decompose under the D4 point group into three
                  orbits of sizes (2, 8, 4), with support classes
                  {64, 48, 32} = {N, V, N/2}, inverse participation ratios
                  {2/128, 3/128, 4/128}, and Shannon entropy classes
                  {6.0, 5.5, 5.0} bits with equal spacing 0.5 bits. The
                  affine entropy-IPR relation S = log2(N) + 1 - N * IPR is
                  proved as a theorem for modes whose squared amplitudes
                  lie in {0, 1/N, 2/N}, and this precondition is verified
                  for every mode in the multiplet.}
